.TH NET-CRAWLER 1 "2026-11-14" "net-docu-crawler 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
net-crawler \- zero-blast-radius multi-vendor network discovery, topology resolution, and documentation engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B net-crawler
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B python3 net_crawler.py
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B net-docu-crawler
(\fBnet-crawler\fR) performs strictly read-only operational state discovery across heterogeneous L2/L3 network infrastructure (switches, routers, firewalls, wireless controllers, and access points) and generates truthful physical (L1/L2) and logical (L3/L4\-7) engineering deliverables.
.PP
Every target flows through a 4-tier identification cascade (local ARP OUI with hypervisor MAC bypass, TCP/22 SSH and TCP/23 Telnet banner inspection, HTTP/TLS fingerprinting, and post-auth prompt/version checks) with vendor-scoped credential ordering to avoid AAA/fail2ban lockouts.
.PP
By default, \fBnet-crawler\fR automatically chases CDP/LLDP neighbor management IPs hop-by-hop without scanning dead user subnets.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-targets " TARGET ..."
One or more target IPs, CIDRs, or \fIip:port\fR specifications (for example \fB10.1.0.1\fR, \fB192.168.1.0/24\fR, or \fB192.168.1.220:2222\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-credentials " FILE ..."
Path(s) to credentials JSON file(s), tried in order. Default: \fBcredentials.json\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-output-dir " DIR"
Flat output directory when \fB\-\-no\-organize\fR is used, or custom base directory when organized. Default flat directory: \fBdocs/net_docu_crawler\fR (default organized base: \fBdeliverables/\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-organize
Store deliverables in a structured subfolder: \fIdeliverables/<Subnet>_<TimeStamp>_<domain>/\fR (default).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-organize
Write flat output directly to \fB\-\-output\-dir\fR without creating a timestamped subfolder.
.TP
.BI \-\-domain " NAME"
Domain/site suffix for organized report folders. Default: \fBlan\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-sanitize\-passwords
Redact passwords, pre-shared keys, and SNMP communities in \fIraw_config\fR, exports, and \fIlogs/*_raw_session.log\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECONDS"
Connection timeout in seconds. Default: \fB8\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-ssh\-ports " PORT ..."
SSH ports to probe during subnet discovery. Default: \fB22\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-telnet\-ports " PORT ..."
Telnet ports to probe during subnet discovery. Default: \fB23\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-workers " N"
Maximum concurrent device crawl workers. Default: \fB16\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-http\-fingerprint
Disable default HTTP/HTTPS banner and TLS certificate fingerprinting for unauthenticated/ARP hosts.
.TP
.B \-\-snmp
Enable opt-in read-only SNMPv2c \fIsysDescr\fR/\fIsysName\fR enrichment for unauthenticated/ARP hosts.
.TP
.BI \-\-snmp\-community " STRING"
SNMPv2c community string when \fB\-\-snmp\fR is enabled. Default: \fBpublic\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-follow\-subnets
Follow directly connected RFC 1918 subnets discovered from crawled routers, switches, and firewalls using harvested ARP entries (falling back to CIDR expansion if no ARP entries exist for a subnet).
.TP
.B \-\-follow\-routes
When \fB\-\-follow\-subnets\fR is enabled, also follow non-connected routing-table prefixes.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-follow\-neighbors
Disable automatic crawling of CDP/LLDP neighbor management IPs discovered on crawled devices.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-hops " N"
Maximum L3 hop depth for neighbor and subnet following. Default: \fB1\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-cgnat
Allow \fB\-\-follow\-subnets\fR to follow CGNAT (\fB100.64.0.0/10\fR) ranges.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-public\-subnets
Allow \fB\-\-follow\-subnets\fR to follow non-RFC1918 public subnets.
.TP
.BI \-\-target\-vendor " VENDOR"
Generate staged target-vendor migration CLI configs (\fBcisco\fR, \fBjuniper\fR, \fBarista\fR, \fBhpprocurve\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-vendor\-hint " VENDOR"
Fallback vendor driver hint when OUI/SSH/Telnet/HTTP detection returns unknown (for example \fBfortinet\fR, \fBhpprocurve\fR, \fBciscosmb\fR, \fBcisco\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-try\-all\-creds
Try all credential profiles even when a specific vendor is detected (not recommended for lockout-protected devices).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-online\-oui
Disable online MAC OUI lookup fallback for unseen prefixes (air-gapped mode).
.TP
.BI \-\-save\-baseline " PATH"
Save pre-cutover baseline state JSON to \fIPATH\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-compare\-baseline " PATH"
Compare current crawl against a saved baseline JSON and generate \fImigration_verification_report.md\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-retry\-failed " PATH"
Path to \fIfailed_hosts.json\fR from a prior run to retry only unauthenticated/missed hosts and merge results back into the run's dataset and reports.
.TP
.BI \-\-from\-dataset " PATH"
Offline mode: reload an existing \fInet_docu_crawler_dataset.json\fR, re-run topology resolution, and regenerate all deliverables with zero network traffic.
.TP
.BI \-\-reparse\-logs " RUN_DIR"
Offline mode: replay \fIlogs/*_raw_session.log\fR in \fIRUN_DIR\fR through the latest vendor drivers and regenerate all deliverables with zero network traffic.
.TP
.B \-\-validate\-credentials
Validate \fB\-\-credentials\fR JSON file(s) and exit without running a crawl.
.SH SUPPORTED VENDORS
Cisco IOS/IOS-XE/NX-OS/IOS-XR, Cisco SMB (SG300/SG350/CBS), Juniper Junos, Arista EOS, ArubaOS-CX / ArubaOS, HP ProCurve / ArubaOS-S (Provision), Fortinet FortiOS, Palo Alto PAN-OS, MikroTik RouterOS, FRRouting, OPNsense, and OpenWrt.
.SH FILES AND DELIVERABLES
Each organized run writes to \fIdeliverables/<Subnet>_<TimeStamp>_<domain>/\fR:
.TP
.I net_docu_crawler_dataset.json
Canonical normalized inventory, interfaces, transceivers, link errors, LLDP/CDP neighbors, routes, ARP/MAC tables, STP, PoE, and DHCP state.
.TP
.I failed_hosts.json
Unauthenticated or unreachable targets for targeted \fB\-\-retry\-failed\fR passes.
.TP
.I Network_Analysis.md
Master network migration blueprint and engineering summary.
.TP
.I net_docu_crawler_live_report.md
Layered L1\-L7 health, STP, CIDR conflict, transceiver, and link-error audit.
.TP
.I L2_network_diagrams.md\fR, \fIL3_network_diagrams.md
Mermaid L1/L2 switching diagrams (with AP overlay) and L3 VLAN/CIDR routing diagrams.
.TP
.I asset_inventory.csv\fR, \fIbom_hardware_sizing.csv\fR, \fImigration_cabling_matrix.csv\fR, \fIport_mac_endpoint_mapping.csv
Structured hardware, optics/PoE BOM, patching, and endpoint-MAC tables.
.TP
.I validate_cutover.sh\fR, \fIvalidate_cutover.ps1
Generated post-cutover smoke-test scripts.
.TP
.I logs/
Audit logs and per-device \fI*_raw_session.log\fR CLI transcripts.
.SH EXAMPLES
Validate \fIcredentials.json\fR before a live run:
.PP
.RS
.nf
python3 net_crawler.py \-\-validate\-credentials
.fi
.RE
.PP
Fast multi-site core/edge crawl chasing CDP/LLDP neighbors without probing user VLANs:
.PP
.RS
.nf
python3 net_crawler.py \-\-targets 10.1.0.1 \-\-max\-hops 3 \-\-workers 12 \-\-timeout 10 \-\-domain campus\-a \-\-organize \-\-sanitize\-passwords
.fi
.RE
.PP
Retry failed hosts after adding credentials:
.PP
.RS
.nf
python3 net_crawler.py \-\-retry\-failed deliverables/10.1.0.1_.../failed_hosts.json \-\-organize \-\-sanitize\-passwords
.fi
.RE
.PP
Re-parse saved raw session logs offline after a driver update:
.PP
.RS
.nf
python3 net_crawler.py \-\-reparse\-logs deliverables/10.1.0.1_.../
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Credential validation failed or an unrecoverable CLI error occurred.
